    "https://employment.uncsa.edu/postings/11068": {
      "title": "Second Year Acting Faculty",
      "description": "University of North Carolina School of the Arts | Second Year Acting Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Review our frequently asked questions Discounts & Perks - UNCSA News at UNCSA Current UNCSA Employee Log in Please use this link to log into PeopleAdmin using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. Second Year Acting Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. An EHRA Faculty application is required in order to be considered for a faculty position. Please note, EHRA Faculty applications do not have an employment entry section. Instead, a resume/CV will be required to be uploaded by the applicant, along with any other documents the Department or assigned Search Committee deem relevant for the review process. Applications will be treated confidentially until the final stages of the search process. The following documents are required to be uploaded with the application; Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References UNCSA follows the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools (SACS) guidelines for faculty credentialing. The successful candidate will be required to submit a curriculum vitae, official transcripts of earned degrees, and/or substantiating documentation of experiential qualifications as a condition of employment. Pursuant to UNCSA policy, as a condition of employment the University must obtain a criminal background report and determine that the nature and seriousness of any criminal offenses do not render employment with the University inappropriate. The University of North Carolina School of the Arts provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination, harassment or retaliation based on race, religion, color, national origin, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, political affiliation, National Guard or veteran status, genetic information, or disability. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Second Year Acting and Directing Faculty Member Position Number 035212 School/Department Information Frequently ranked as one of the best drama schools in the world, the School of Drama at UNCSA , prepares talented young artists for successful careers on stage, online, and in film and television. Conservatory training grounded in classical values adds technical skills to shape creatively inspired and versatile actors who are in-demand in today’s evolving entertainment landscape. Position Summary The UNCSA School of Drama seeks a dynamic teacher of acting who is prepared to join our second-year acting sequence wherein our students are engaged in a series of rehearsal processes that culminate in a stripped-down workshop play presentation – not a public performance. Building on a strong first-year foundation, this teacher will guide our students further into text analysis while keeping them rooted in physical impulse/storytelling. The second-year acting faculty are tasked with directing our students through a series of increasingly theatricalized plays each quarter – contemporary realism, contemporary with heightened theatricality, period and style, and finishing with something absurdist or expressionistic in nature. By exposing our students to a wide variety of material, it is our goal to make them employable across all genres and styles. Description of Responsibilities and Duties This teacher will also be expected to teach a Special Topics course that fits within their area of expertise. Experience teaching improvisation, entertainment industry awareness, and the ability to help facilitate industry guests are greatly welcome. This position also holds the potential to direct within our main-stage season. The ideal candidate has at least five years teaching at the collegiate level, professional experience within the entertainment industry, is ready to train exceptional young actors selected through a highly competitive audition process, and is excited to evolve the training program forward. The person hired in this position must be collegial and willing to serve within the greater community of the university through committee work. Required Qualifications The UNCSA School of Drama recognizes that not all teaching is done in a traditional classroom setting and we are able to hire artists based on their work experience; therefore, we encourage all that are interested to apply. Faculty teaching undergraduate level courses must possess: Earned doctorate/master’s degree in the teaching discipline or a related discipline or earned master’s degree with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in the teaching discipline OR Equivalent professional/experiential qualifications OR Equivalent combination of education and professional experience. Preferred Qualifications Tenure Information UNCSA utilizes a multi-year contract system in lieu of tenure. Instructions to Candidates APPLICATION PROCESS The review of applications will commence on 12/1/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, all application materials must be received by Monday, November 30, 2026. The following documents are required to be uploaded with the application; Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References More information about the school can be found online at www.uncsa.edu/drama, and information about Winston-Salem can be found at www.winstonsalem.com. Classification Code Posting Detail Information Posting Number F131P Open Date 10/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Recruitment Range, if applicable $68,000 - $75,000 Special Instructions to Candidates An EHRA Faculty application is required in order to be considered for a faculty position. Please note, EHRA Faculty applications do not have an employment entry section. Instead, a resume/CV will be required to be uploaded by the applicant, along with any other documents the Department or assigned Search Committee deem relevant for the review process. Applications will be treated confidentially until the final stages of the search process. The following documents are required to be uploaded with the application; Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References UNCSA follows the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools ( SACS ) guidelines for faculty credentialing. The successful candidate will be required to submit a curriculum vitae, official transcripts of earned degrees, and/or substantiating documentation of experiential qualifications as a condition of employment. Pursuant to UNCSA policy, as a condition of employment the University must obtain a criminal background report and determine that the nature and seriousness of any criminal offenses do not render employment with the University inappropriate. The University of North Carolina School of the Arts provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination, harassment or retaliation based on race, religion, color, national origin, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, political affiliation, National Guard or veteran status, genetic information, or disability. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you learn about this employment opportunity? UNCSA Website Agency Referral Print Advertisement (Newspaper / Periodical) Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, Facebook, Other) Online Job Board Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 University of North Carolina School of the Arts 1533 South Main St. Winston Salem, NC 27127 336-770-3399 Privacy Copyright © 2021 UNCSA. All Rights reserved To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
