l to direct within our main-stage season. The ideal candidate has at least five years teaching at the collegiate level, professional experience within the entertainment industry, is ready to train exceptional young actors selected through a highly competitive audition process, and is excited to evolve the training program forward. The person hired in this position must be collegial and willing to serve within the greater community of the university through committee work. Required Qualifications The UNCSA School of Drama recognizes that not all teaching is done in a traditional classroom setting and we are able to hire artists based on their work experience; therefore, we encourage all that are interested to apply. Faculty teaching undergraduate level courses must possess: Earned doctorate/master’s degree in the teaching discipline or a related discipline or earned master’s degree with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in the teaching discipline OR Equivalent professional/experiential qualifications OR Equivalent combination of education and professional experience. Preferred Qualifications Tenure Information UNCSA utilizes a multi-year contract system in lieu of tenure. Instructions to Candidates APPLICATION PROCESS The review of applications will commence on 12/1/2026 and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, all application materials must be received by Monday, November 30, 2026. The following documents are required to be uploaded with the application; Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References More information about the school can be found online at www.uncsa.edu/drama, and information about Winston-Salem can be found at www.winstonsalem.com. Classification Code Posting Detail Information Posting Number F131P Open Date 10/26/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Recruitment Range, if applicable $68,000 - $75,000 Special Instructions to Candidates An EHRA Faculty application is required in order to be considered for